Own and grow the merchant portfolio, identifying and closing cross-sell and upsell opportunities to meet or exceed revenue targets;
Lead commercial negotiations with clients, balancing their needs with EBANX's commercial goals — making it a Win-Win result;
A deep understanding of the client’s business model and business needs; design and deliver merchant-specific growth strategies leveraging data, market intel, payment landscape etc.;
Build and sustain trusted, long-term relationships with senior merchant stakeholders, acting as a strategic advisor;
Conduct regular performance reviews with clients to identify gaps, propose improvements, and co-create roadmaps for growth;
Collaborate cross-functionally with product, operations, legal, and compliance teams to resolve issues and deliver a seamless merchant experience;
Translate complex payment and regulatory topics into clear, actionable guidance for merchants navigating LATAM markets for the first time;
Manage your pipeline rigorously in Salesforce, using data to prioritize and forecast with accuracy

Mandarin as a native language; fluent English; Korean is a plus
7+ years in account management or business development, with demonstrated experience managing senior-level client relationships in e-commerce, OTA, gaming, or related verticals;
7+ years of payment industry knowledge of payment processing flow, card scheme policy, chargeback and fraud management, card payment, local alternative payment methods etc.;
Proven track record of hitting and exceeding revenue targets in a growth-stage or fast-moving environment;
Strong analytical mindset: comfortable working with data to build a case, spot an opportunity, or challenge an assumption;
Bachelor's degree in Business, Economics, or related field;
Overseas living or study experience preferred — comfort operating across cultures is essential in this role;
Flexible availability to accommodate China, US and LATAM time zone overlap

